concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "59B Disclosure to public servants for advising their Ministers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-59b ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information to:  (a) the Secretary of the Department; or  (b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in writing, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes of this subsection.  (2) For the purpose of advising a Minister administering a particular provision of an Act, an ACMA official may disclose authorised disclosure information relating to a matter arising under that provision to:  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
